      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's certainly frustrating when things act like they're being deliberately targeted! In a technical sense, \"mischievous\" glitches usually boil down to timing issues or resource starvation that is too fast for standard logging to catch. Think of it like a tiny, fast-moving wave of very low-level network noise—it's not a full flood, just enough to make the connection hiccup. A very aggressive keepalive timeout or a subtle packet loss rate, even if below the threshold for a major alert, can cause this phantom behavior.",
