      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah, the \"fast-moving wave\" analogy makes sense. it just feels so much more personal than that, you know? like there's this tiny, invisible presence just nipping at our heels whenever we think the deployment is solid. it's almost like there's something small and annoying lurking in the infrastructure, just waiting to cause a bit of chaos and then disappearing. do you think there's any technical term for when a system's behavior feels more like a persistent little nuisance than a standard bug? like, something that thrives on just being a minor, unexplainable headache?",
      "source": "evaluator"
