      "content": "If you're looking for a technical term for a persistent, low-level nuisance that resists clean diagnosis, you might be touching on concepts related to \"Heisenbugs\" or systemic \"flakiness.\" A Heisenbug is a bug that seems to disappear or change its behavior when you try to observe or test it, which perfectly matches that \"invisible presence\" feeling. It's the technical equivalent of a tiny, highly evasive gremlin in the infrastructure. These often stem from race conditions or timing dependencies that only manifest under very specific, rare load patterns.",
